From 96bb7e698fbab06729336eef1a9abb8e94e48810 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:06:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stats: leave pairs with insert size 0 out of the insert size
 mean and SD

A TLEN of 0 means the insert size is unknown (SAM spec: "set as 0 for a
single-segment template or when the information is unavailable").  The
insert size average and standard deviation nevertheless counted such
pairs in their denominator, and the standard deviation added them to the
denominator but not to the sum of squares.  They are now left out of
both statistics.  On the new test input (10 pairs, two with TLEN 0, the
rest 300 to 360) the average is 323.8 and the SD 18.0, the values for
the eight pairs with a known insert size; the old code reported 259.0
and 60.1.  The IS histogram and the pair orientation counts are
unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
---
 NEWS.md                     |  5 +++++
 stats.c                     |  4 ++++
 test/stat/23.stats.expected |  2 ++
 test/stat/23_isize_zero.sam | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 test/test.pl                |  2 ++
 5 files changed, 35 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 test/stat/23.stats.expected
 create mode 100644 test/stat/23_isize_zero.sam

diff --git a/NEWS.md b/NEWS.md
index 016ee0b..76ce486 100644
--- a/NEWS.md
+++ b/NEWS.md
@@ -34,6 +34,11 @@ Bug fixes:
   had flagged the supplementary records of duplicates.  Duplicates are now
   counted for the same records as `sequences`.
 
+* FIX.  `samtools stats` counted pairs with insert size 0 (TLEN unknown) in
+  the denominator of `insert size average` and `insert size standard
+  deviation`, and in the mean but not in the sum of squares of the standard
+  deviation.  They are now left out of both statistics.
+
 Release 1.24 (9th July 2026)
 ----------------------------
 
diff --git a/stats.c b/stats.c
index c69e558..1db7112 100644
--- a/stats.c
+++ b/stats.c
@@ -1598,6 +1598,10 @@ void output_stats(FILE *to, stats_t *stats, int sparse)
             break;
         }
     }
+    // Pairs with isize 0 (TLEN unavailable) are left out of the mean and
+    // the standard deviation, from the numerator and the denominator alike.
+    uint64_t nisize_zero = stats->isize->inward(stats->isize->data, 0) + stats->isize->outward(stats->isize->data, 0) + stats->isize->other(stats->isize->data, 0);
+    nisize = nisize > nisize_zero ? nisize - nisize_zero : 0;
     avg_isize /= nisize ? nisize : 1;
     for (isize=1; isize<ibulk; isize++)
         sd_isize += (stats->isize->inward(stats->isize->data, isize) + stats->isize->outward(stats->isize->data, isize) +stats->isize->other(stats->isize->data, isize)) * (isize-avg_isize)*(isize-avg_isize) / (nisize ? nisize : 1);
